      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1950, residents renamed it Crestview through a civic contest, paving the way for formal incorporation later that year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/crestview_kentucky",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Originally developed from former farmland, the landscape has transitioned primarily to residential use.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/crestview_kentucky",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Its proximity to the Ohio River, about 5 miles away, boosts local humidity and supports riparian wetlands and forest corridors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
